jobs.description:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sail is Stripe’s user interface platform and design system. We build the design language, components, tools, and front-end foundations that product teams use to create coherent, accessible, responsive, and high-quality experiences. Designers on Sail work closely with engineers and designers across Stripe to turn recurring product needs into durable solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Designer on Sail, you’ll contribute to the visual and interaction foundations of Stripe’s products. With support from experienced designers and engineers, you’ll work on scoped components, patterns, guidance, and tools. This role is a good fit for a designer who cares deeply about visual craft, enjoys thinking in systems, and wants to understand how design decisions become production interfaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and refine user interface components, patterns, and foundations for use across Stripe products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create polished, coherent interfaces across interaction states, themes, and responsive layouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with front-end engineers to understand constraints and carry designs into production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Figma libraries, prototypes, specifications, documentation, and examples&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather input from product teams, share work, and iterate based on feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience designing digital products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio demonstrating strong visual design craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using or contributing to a design system or component library&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with front-end engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working understanding of components, states, and responsive behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using artificial intelligence tools in day-to-day design work, with familiarity with large language models, agents, and reusable skills or workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating or maintaining user interface components or shared design libraries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of HTML and CSS, with experience using artificial intelligence and prototyping tools to build and evaluate interactive interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing native mobile interfaces for iOS or Android&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Figma is growing our team of passionate creatives and builders on a mission to make design accessible to all. Figma’s platform helps teams bring ideas to life—whether you&#39;re brainstorming, creating a prototype, translating designs into code, or iterating with AI. From idea to product, Figma empowers teams to streamline workflows, move faster, and work together in real time from anywhere in the world. If you&#39;re excited to shape the future of design and collaboration, join us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a technically-minded product designer who is excited to shape how design, code, and AI-powered workflows come together at Figma. In this role, you&#39;ll improve how Figma understands production code and design systems, design workflows that move from design to code and back again, and extend Figma&#39;s agentic capabilities into developer tools and the places teams already work. You&#39;ll turn ambiguity into clarity alongside engineers, PMs, and researchers, bringing simplicity and craft to complex technical problems as we help define the future of how software is made.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time role that can be held from our London hub or remotely within the UK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do at Figma:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape and prototype new workflows that bring design and production code closer together, including AI-powered experiences that connect Figma with the tools teams already use to build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to overall strategy and decision-making about product direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help deliver and refine clear storytelling around product needs and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with product management, engineering, UX writing, data science, and research peers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and iterate on flows, prototypes, and high-fidelity visuals, as well as provide thoughtful feedback for others doing the same so you can all do your best work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and ship high-quality features and product improvements in Figma&#39;s core product surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to our design org&#39;s culture by participating in design critiques, mentoring peers, and sharing best practices across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;d love to hear from you if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience designing UX and UI for software products of similar scale and complexity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong visual craft and attention to detail across composition, typography, layout, interaction design, and prototyping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to independently drive end-to-end design processes from discovery through launch, balancing user needs, technical constraints, and business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to guide decision-making through structured thinking, clear design rationale, and user-centered research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing technically complex products, ideally developer tools or extensible platforms, with an understanding of software development workflows, APIs, and systems; experience prototyping and evaluating AI-powered or nondeterministic interactions is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;While it&#39;s not required, it&#39;s an added plus if you also have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with web technologies like HTML/CSS, AI coding tools such as Codex, Cursor, or Claude Code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of advanced Figma features like Auto Layout, Variables, and Components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building with web technologies, APIs, CLIs, MCP, model evals, or other tools used to create developer and AI products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A history of working on canvas-based interfaces or tools that support creative workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work involving design systems, like creating, maintaining, or contributing to a design system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;At Figma, one of our values is Grow as you go. We believe in hiring smart, curious people who are excited to learn and develop their skills. If you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with the points outlined in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Figma we celebrate and support our differences. We know employing a team rich in diverse thoughts, experiences, and opinions allows our employees, our product and our community to flourish. Figma is an &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2022-10/EEOC_KnowYourRights_screen_reader_10_20.pdf&quot;&gt;equal opportunity workplace&lt;/a&gt; - we are dedicated to equal employment opportunities regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity/expression, veteran status&lt;strong&gt;, &lt;/strong&gt;or any other characteristic protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will work to ensure individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to apply for a role, participate in the interview process, perform essential job functions, and receive other benefits and privileges of employment. If you require accommodation, please reach out to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:accommodations-ext@figma.com&quot;&gt;accommodations-ext@figma.com&lt;/a&gt;. These modifications enable an individual with a disability to have an equal opportunity not only to get a job, but successfully perform their job tasks to the same extent as people without disabilities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Examples of accommodations include but are not limited to:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Holding interviews in an accessible location&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enabling closed captioning on video conferencing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring all written communication be compatible with screen readers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Changing the mode or format of interviews&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To ensure the integrity of our hiring process and facilitate a more personal connection, we require all candidates keep their cameras on during video interviews. Additionally, if hired you will be required to attend in person onboarding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By applying for this job, the candidate acknowledges and agrees that any personal data contained in their application or supporting materials will be processed in accordance with &lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.figma.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.figma.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Figma&#39;s Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;About The Opportunity&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Senior Manager, Product Design to lead a team of product designers working across some of Contentful’s most foundational product areas: content performance optimization, application platform capabilities, business foundations, and design systems. Contentful is the composable content platform powering how the world&#39;s leading brands create, manage, and deliver digital experiences. These teams enable our platform&#39;s evolution as we build AI native features — turning ambitious product strategy into intuitive, well-crafted experiences for the customers and partners who build on Contentful every day. You&#39;ll balance strategic design leadership with people management: coaching designers, raising the bar on craft, and ensuring design has a strong voice in how these foundational parts of the platform take shape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;What To Expect?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll manage designers across three product areas: content performance optimization, application platform capabilities, business infrastructure, and design systems. Optimization, Application Foundations and Business Foundations. While all teams strive to deliver solutions for a holistic, unified platform, each has a distinct focus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our Optimization group focuses on advancing personalization and analytics capabilities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our Application Foundations group includes design systems &amp;amp; information architecture, as well as workflows &amp;amp; automation tooling, and search &amp;amp; discoverability. Notably, the Contentful platform is built on our open source design system, Forma 36.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Business Foundations group focuses on identity &amp;amp; access, monetization, and platform insights.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll manage a team of designers you can genuinely invest in — coaching career growth, shaping how they work, and giving them real ownership over their piece of the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll partner directly with product and engineering leadership on strategy, not just execution to shape how Optimization, Application Foundations, and Business Foundations evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll help define what AI-native design leadership looks like at Contentful, at a moment when the company is actively maturing that muscle. The Contentful platform includes AI powered customer facing features, and accordingly, we progressively evolve our design tooling and ways of working to take advantage of emerging technologies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can be located in or near our London hub. The product designers you manage will be located in EMEA as well, distributed across London, Dublin and our Berlin headquarters. Your manager will be US based and you will collaborate with colleagues globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some travel is expected. The organization typically has training and/or workshops located in our Berlin headquarters, approximately quarterly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will be joining at a pivotal moment: Contentful&#39;s recent acquisition by Salesforce puts this team&#39;s work in front of a massive new customer base, giving you a rare chance to help shape design at a large scale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Need To Be Successful&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of product design experience, including 3+ years directly managing and developing product designers, ideally at a B2B SaaS or platform company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of partnering with product and engineering leadership at the strategy level, not just translating requirements. You will influence roadmap decisions, represent design&#39;s perspective in cross-functional planning, and drive visioning initiatives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong customer-centric orientation. You ground design and product decisions in real customer insights and instill that same instinct across your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of design leadership that extends beyond your own team. Experience shaping and evolving the product design function’s practices within an organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a high bar for design craft, with a portfolio reflecting strong interaction and visual design fundamentals. You set and uphold that same bar across your team by giving specific, actionable feedback that sharpens execution, not just strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of leading design for complex, multi-team product areas. You should influence a coherent vision that translates across teams supporting a unified platform.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning or contributing to a design system at scale; familiarity with design systems like Forma 36.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success managing distributed, global teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in AI-native product design, including shipping AI-powered customer-facing features, as well as evolving design tooling and workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong portfolio evidence of coaching designers&#39; career growth. Experience facilitating promotions, skill development, and performance management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a technically complex, enterprise/platform context. The interfaces and user flows we design operate within a headless, API first context and a mindset of ‘systems thinking’ is paramount.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More details about our company benefits can be found at the following link:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;link__new-tab&quot; href=&quot;https://www.salesforcebenefits.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://www.salesforcebenefits.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contentful is now officially part of Salesforce.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Unleash Your Potential&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you join Salesforce, you’ll be limitless in all areas of your life. Our benefits and resources support you to find balance and be your best, and our AI agents accelerate your impact so you can do your best. Together, we’ll bring the power of Agentforce to organizations of all sizes and deliver amazing experiences that customers love. Apply today to not only shape the future — but to redefine what’s possible — for yourself, for AI, and the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you need reasonable accommodations at any point during the application or interview process, please let your Recruiter know.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salesforce is an equal opportunity employer and maintains a policy of non-discrimination with all employees and applicants for employment. What does that mean exactly? It means that at Salesforce, we believe in equality for all. And we believe we can lead the path to equality in part by creating a workplace that’s inclusive, and free from discrimination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/know-your-rights-workplace-discrimination-illegal&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Know your rights: workplace discrimination is illegal.&lt;/a&gt; Any employee or potential employee will be assessed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications – without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender expression or identity, transgender status, age, disability, veteran or marital status, political viewpoint, or other classifications protected by law. This policy applies to current and prospective employees, no matter where they are in their Salesforce employment journey. It also applies to recruiting, hiring, job assignment, compensation, promotion, benefits, training, assessment of job performance, discipline, termination, and everything in between. Recruiting, hiring, and promotion decisions at Salesforce are fair and based on merit. The same goes for compensation, benefits, promotions, transfers, reduction in workforce, recall, training, and education.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #3e3e3e;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please be aware of scammers who may fraudulently claim to be from Contentful. These types of fraud can occur through copycat websites, fake email addresses claiming to be from our company, or social media. We do not ask for your personal information, such as bank account numbers, identification numbers, etc., through social media or chat-based apps, nor do we request or send money to purchase business equipment. If you suspect fraud, please report it to your local authorities and contact us at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:security-esk@contentful.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;security-esk@contentful.com&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #3e3e3e;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;with any information you may have.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;By clicking “Apply for this job,” I acknowledge that I have read the “&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.contentful.com/legal/us/privacy-notice-to-candidates/privacy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Contentful’s Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;” and hereby consent to the collection, processing, use, and storage of my personal information as described therein.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;🚀 We’re on a mission to make money work for everyone.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re waving goodbye to the complicated and confusing ways of traditional banking.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After starting as a prepaid card, our product offering has grown a lot in the last 10 years in the UK. As well as&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/current-account/personal&quot;&gt;personal&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/business-banking&quot;&gt;business&lt;/a&gt; bank accounts, we offer &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/current-account/joint-account&quot;&gt;joint accounts&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/current-account/16-17&quot;&gt;accounts for 16-17 year olds&lt;/a&gt;, a &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/current-account/under-16s&quot;&gt;free kids account&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/flex&quot;&gt;credit cards&lt;/a&gt; in the UK, with more exciting things to come beyond. Our UK customers can also &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/savings&quot;&gt;save&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/investments&quot;&gt;invest &lt;/a&gt;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/pensions&quot;&gt;combine their pensions&lt;/a&gt; with us.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With our hot coral cards and get-paid-early feature, combined with financial education on social media and our award winning customer service, we have a long history of creating magical moments for our customers!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re not about selling products - we want to solve problems and change lives through Monzo ❤️&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;📍London (Hybrid) / UK Remote | 💰 £90,000 - £120,000 + Incentive Awards tied to your performance +&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/careers#benefits&quot;&gt; Benefits&lt;/a&gt; ✨&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;⭐Our Design team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a team of 115+ designers, researchers, and brand experts led by Chief Design Officer Vuokko Aro. We’re on a mission to make money work for everyone. Product Design makes up over half of our design disciplines, working in tight-knit squads alongside research, product, engineering and data to solve real customer problems at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We design for the &quot;magic moments&quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ve built a bank that feels human, not just functional. Our product &lt;em&gt;is&lt;/em&gt; our personality. We blend research, empathy, data and craft to turn everyday interactions into memorable experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Right now, we’re growing fast and looking for passionate designers to shape Monzo’s future — and there’s a huge opportunity to make your mark.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌱 About Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Growth collective is focused on helping more people discover Monzo, understand what makes us different, and find the products that can make money work better for them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For this role, you’ll have a particular focus on our &lt;strong&gt;web experiences&lt;/strong&gt;, helping us rethink how people discover, explore and choose Monzo before they ever open the app. You’ll combine strong visual and interaction design with a data-informed mindset, using experimentation and customer insight to understand what works and continuously improve the experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don’t need to have worked in a dedicated Growth team before. We’re interested in designers who are curious about customer behaviour, comfortable using data to inform their decisions, and excited by the opportunity to apply exceptional craft to high-impact customer journeys.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🔑You’ll play a key role by...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading the design of high-quality web experiences that help new and existing customers discover the value Monzo can bring to their financial lives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using quantitative and qualitative data to identify opportunities, understand customer behaviour and make informed design decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turning customer and business problems into clear hypotheses, designing experiments and using what you learn to shape what we do next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bringing exceptional visual and interaction craft to our web experiences, creating work that feels unmistakably Monzo while driving meaningful customer and commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tackling complex and ambiguous design challenges, balancing customer needs, business goals and technical constraints to create simple, effective experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Defining compelling product visions and direction, helping teams think beyond individual experiments towards a coherent long-term customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering closely with Product, Engineering, Data and Research throughout the design process, bringing people together around customer problems and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using AI to level-up parts of your design workflow. Whether that’s ideation, analysis, prototyping or shipping production code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking a pragmatic approach to experimentation — moving quickly when we need to learn, while knowing when an experience needs a higher level of craft and polish.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acting as a role model in Design, sharing your work broadly, mentoring others, and contributing to the growth and success of the wider Design team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🤩 We’d love to hear from you if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a proven track record of designing &lt;strong&gt;high-quality web experiences&lt;/strong&gt;, with a portfolio that demonstrates strong visual and interaction design craft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable using &lt;strong&gt;data to inform your design decisions&lt;/strong&gt;, partnering with Data Scientists or Analysts to understand customer behaviour and measure the impact of your work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can connect great customer experiences with measurable outcomes and understand how design can contribute to wider product and commercial goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable forming hypotheses, experimenting with different approaches and adapting your thinking as you learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can balance speed and experimentation with a high bar for craft, knowing when to prototype quickly and when to invest in creating an exceptional final experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a natural collaborator who can bring together Product, Engineering, Data, Research and other partners around complex customer problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in ambiguity and can create clarity and direction when the answer isn’t immediately obvious.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable thinking beyond an individual screen or experiment, connecting work across journeys and helping shape a longer-term vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a role model who actively contributes to the growth of the Design team through mentoring, feedback and sharing your expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re excited about Monzo’s mission to make money work for everyone and the opportunity to help more people discover the value of Monzo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🙌What’s in it for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰 £90,000 - £110,000 + Incentive Awards tied to your performance.&lt;br&gt;✈️ We’ll help you relocate to the UK.&lt;br&gt;✅ We can sponsor your visa.&lt;br&gt;📍This role can be based in our London office, but we&#39;re open to distributed working within the UK (with ad hoc meetings in London).&lt;br&gt;⏰We offer flexible working hours and trust you to work enough hours to do your job well, and at times that suit you and your team.&lt;br&gt;📚£1,000 learning budget each year to use on books, training courses and conferences.&lt;br&gt;🏡We will set you up to work from home; all employees are given Macbooks and for fully remote workers we will provide extra support for your work-from-home setup.&lt;br&gt;➕ Plus lots more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌈 &lt;strong&gt;The application journey has 3 key steps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30-minute call with our Recruiter, Tom&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-hour craft interview where you’ll present a single case study to 2 members of our Design team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 x 45-minute interviews covering Teamwork and Impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This process should take around 4 weeks - your schedule is really important to us, so we promise to be as flexible as possible!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have some guidelines on using Artificial Intelligence (AI) to ace an application and interview at Monzo.&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/the-ultimate-guide-on-using-ai-to-ace-an-interview-at-monzo&quot;&gt; You can read them here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ll only close this role once we have enough applications for the next stage. Please submit your application as soon as possible to make sure you don’t miss out.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-TR1&lt;br&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunities for everyone&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Diversity and inclusion are a priority for us and we’re making sure we have lots of support for all of our people to grow at Monzo. At Monzo, we’re embracing diversity by fostering an inclusive environment for all people to do the best work of their lives with us. This is integral to our mission of making money work for everyone. You can read more in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/diversity-and-inclusion&quot;&gt;blog&lt;/a&gt;, 2026 &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/our-2026-diversity-and-inclusion-report&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Diversity and Inclusion Report&lt;/a&gt; and 2025 &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/gender-pay-gap-report-2025&quot;&gt;Gender Pay Gap Report.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer. All applicants will be considered for employment without attention to age, ethnicity, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, family or parental status, national origin, or veteran, neurodiversity or disability status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a preferred name, please use it to apply. We don&#39;t need full or birth names at application stage 😊&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

THE WORLD’S MOST ADVANCED VPN, AND A WHOLE LOT MORE.

If you’re a curious problem-solver who carves their own path, join the team behind Threat Protection Pro, the NordLynx protocol, and the fastest VPN on the planet—tools that put privacy, security, and control back in people’s hands.

Your impact? Helping millions take back control of their online security, privacy, and data.




MAIN RESPONSIBILITIES

 - Full ownership of feedback sources for product quality issues; 

 - Roadmap for detection and prevention improvements;

 - Prioritization of issues for resolution;

 - Collaboration with product owners, engineers, and other stakeholders, identification of blockers, management of dependencies and resources;

 - Monitoring and continuous iteration on detection performance;

 - Reporting results and status to upper management and other stakeholders;

 - Align objectives, expectations, and timeframes among developers, designers, product, and business stakeholders;

 - Embrace transparency and communication.

 


CORE REQUIREMENTS

 - Proven experience working as a product owner, IT project manager, or Product manager;

 - Proven experience in working with development teams;

 - Proven experience in identifying deliverable dependencies, roadblocks, or challenges;

 - Strong technical understanding of how software is built, deployed, and maintained;

 - Excellent interpersonal and communication skills;

 - Solid organizational skills, including attention to detail and multitasking skills;

 - Leadership, Risk Management, Critical Thinking, Analytical Skills.



 


WHAT WE OFFER

 - Sharpen your edge: training, mentorship, and room to grow — always.



 - Take the time you need: extra vacation days, sick days, and time off when life calls.



 - Get premium healthcare: private health insurance in Lithuania and Poland — fully covered.



 - Protect your peace: enjoy free subscriptions to Calm, Headspace, and Mindletic, and our own resilience and mindfulness trainings.



 - Own your fitness: in-house gyms, sport cards, online workouts, and personal guidance — on us.



 - Pack your bags for workation: experience our company-wide trip abroad to the fullest.



 - Work from anywhere: work from wherever keeps you in the zone.



 - Celebrate your milestones: birthdays, weddings, and new family members — all deserve a gift.



 - Parent with ease: children’s summer camps and flexibility around the schedule — because parenting never pauses.



 - Join the party: team building and company events people talk about for months.



 - Unlock Cyber City: coffee bar, open gyms, kids’ room, music room, massage chairs — our Vilnius HQ is yours to enjoy.





